{"user": "what are the important strategies for opening moves?", "user_ts": "2026-08-19T11:11:11.778124+00:00", "assistant": "Key opening strategies in Othello:\n\n- **Don\u2019t chase flips early.** Flipping many discs early often gives your opponent more moves.\n- **Aim for mobility.** Try to leave yourself many legal moves and your opponent few.\n- **Play toward the center.** Early stable, quiet moves near the middle are usually safer.\n- **Avoid X-squares early**: **b2, g2, b7, g7** \u2014 diagonal to corners. They often give away corners.\n- **Avoid C-squares carelessly**: squares next to corners like **a2, b1, g1, h2**, etc. They can also hand over corners.\n- **Corners are huge.** A corner disc can never be flipped, so getting corners usually matters more than gaining discs now.\n- **Build stable edges only when safe.** Taking an edge too early can become a weakness if it gives access to corners.\n- **Think one move ahead:** \u201cIf I play here, what good move do I give White?\u201d\n\nSimple opening mindset: **stay compact, keep mobility, avoid giving corner access.**", "assistant_started_ts": "2026-08-19T11:11:13.317577+00:00", "assistant_ts": "2026-08-19T11:11:18.060779+00:00", "annotation_user": {"final": ["Knowledge Deficit Question"], "consensus": ["Knowledge Deficit Question"], "votes": {"Solution Request": 1, "Knowledge Deficit Question": 2}, "confidence": {"Solution Request": 0.3333333333333333, "Knowledge Deficit Question": 0.6666666666666666}, "per_model": {"gpt": ["Solution Request"], "sonnet": ["Knowledge Deficit Question"], "llama": ["Knowledge Deficit Question"]}, "n_valid": 3, "min_votes": 2, "no_majority": false, "needs_review": false, "arbiter_used": false}, "annotation_assistant_fine": {"final": ["General Principle"], "consensus": ["General Principle"], "votes": {"General Principle": 3}, "confidence": {"General Principle": 1.0}, "per_model": {"gpt": ["General Principle"], "llama": ["General Principle"], "sonnet": ["General Principle"]}, "n